# Launch timeline compliance

Canonical schedule: [`LAUNCH_TIMELINE.md`](../../LAUNCH_TIMELINE.md).
Earliest production target: **~Aug 22, 2026**.

## After every user prompt

Before or at the end of the response, run a **tiny compliance check** (2–4 lines max unless the user asked about launch):

1. **Today’s window** — which row of the timeline applies (use user_info date).
2. **On track / at risk** — one line; flag if work contradicts the window (e.g. building features instead of device QA during Jul 25–28).
3. **Critical path** — from Jul 28 onward, remind that **recruiting 12 testers** runs in parallel with listing/build; don’t serialize it.
4. **Out of scope for this launch** — don’t suggest sync/FCM/accounts/cert pinning as launch blockers unless the user expands scope.

Skip the check only if the user message is purely meta (e.g. “ignore timeline”) or a one-word ack with no work.

## Window cheat sheet

| Dates | Focus |
|---|---|
| Jul 25–28 | Device QA, bug pass, verify v1 issues fixed (checkbox, voice, image) |
| Jul 28–30 | Signed AAB, Play listing, privacy policy |
| Jul 30–31 | Internal testing — self sanity-check |
| Jul 28+ parallel | Recruit 12 closed testers |
| ~Aug 1 | Closed testing → 14-day clock |
| ~Aug 15 | Apply for production access |
| ~Aug 15–22 | Google review |
| ~Aug 22 | Earliest production |

## When user asks “what next?”

Answer from the **current window** in `LAUNCH_TIMELINE.md`, not a generic backlog.
